{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented and pushed for review as Gerrit change 3131 (commit 44147abf0251164cbc8f3d77c9838978d88e9d30), based on origin/main f8ddcaf88e6.\n\nAcceptance criteria measured against the worktree:\n\n- AC1 `test -e src/rebar/llm/aggregate.py` -> exit 1. PASS\n- AC2 tree-wide `aggregate_findings` grep -> no output, exit 1. PASS\n- AC3 `_severity_rank` appears only in `spec_scan.py` (definition :25, call :143). PASS\n- AC4 `aggregate_findings` absent from the `rebar.llm` namespace. PASS\n- AC5 release-notes entry present. PASS\n- AC6 `make verify` -> exit 0, 19826 passed, 88 skipped, 52m43s. PASS\n\nNotes for review:\n\n- `_severity_rank` moved verbatim into `spec_scan.py` beside its only call site rather\n  than into a new shared helper. It is two lines plus a rank dict, and a new module would\n  re-create the one-caller indirection this slice removes.\n- `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json` needed no update: it never carried an `aggregate`\n  entry, so deleting the module does not move the recorded public surface. The surface gate\n  passes unchanged (18 passed).\n- The complexity and mechanism ratchets both report the deletion as `stale`, which is the\n  allowed shrink direction, not a regression.\n\nThe verify run took 52m43s against the documented 20-25 min. A parallel session was running\nits own gates on this host throughout, so the spread is consistent with host contention\nrather than anything in this change; the test selection and pass count are unchanged."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793241840455073961,"uuid":"beac6e34-a52a-4a6b-90e8-eea25c02c7fd"}